Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 23:38:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11362/11362] Two of ten compaction rebuilds made the prompt
 BIGGER, and nothing counts it

Found by chasing sk48, the one cell that records compactions: 1 while its
prompt_tokens_per_turn never drops. Replaying the shipped controller over
each ON cell's own measured sequence recovers the exact fire turns, and
reproduces the recorded compactions counter on 13 of 13 cells.

  lp85 turn 7: 18754 -> 21730 (+2976)
  sk48 turn 7: 17335 -> 20451 (+3116)

A rebuild is base + carried state + one full tail round. When the base is
small (sk48 8531, lp85 9074) and the tail round is a large tool result, that
sum can exceed the transcript it replaces. The event then pays the
re-prefill and buys negative context.

No counter reports it. compact_floor_hit was false on both cells, so the
existing telemetry calls them healthy. The consequence is bounded rather
than runaway, because the thrash floor then raises the threshold off the
new larger post-rebuild size, so a bad rebuild delays the next event instead
of looping. The cheapest fix is to compare the rebuilt size against the
current one, skip the event when it would not shrink, and count the skip.
Raised as an operator decision rather than made, since it is a code change
to a default-off flag.

This also sharpens G-M. The aggregate claim holds -- peak prompt tokens
-26.3% on the cells that fire -- but it does not hold per event: 20% of
events were counterproductive and invisible.

Side benefit: the 13/13 agreement between the replay and the recorded
counters is a second falsification control for the note's headline. The same
instrument that reports 0 firings at 4 turns agrees with ground truth
everywhere ground truth exists, including all 7 non-zero cells. If
compaction did fire at 4 turns, that control would have disagreed.

Note and ledger verdict both corrected in place; the corrections are stated
as corrections, not silently folded in.

